---
// src/pages/ai-network-operations.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="AI-Assisted Network Operations & Automation | InfraHub"
  description="Evaluate AI-assisted network operations, source-of-truth-driven automation, incident context, and operational workflows with specialist network partners."
  canonicalPath="/ai-network-operations"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container service-container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <div class="header-badge-row">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-blue">AIOps & Automation</span>
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Delivered</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="service-title">AI-Assisted Network Operations</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          Use network context, automation, and AI-assisted workflows to help engineers investigate incidents, reduce repetitive handling, and connect operational actions to a reliable source of truth. InfraHub helps define where this approach fits before introducing an appropriate specialist.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=ai-netops" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request AIOps Evaluation</a>
          <a href="/partners/itcare" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Explore ITcare</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Operational Workflows</span>
        <h2>Where AI-Assisted Operations Can Fit</h2>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Incident Context</h3>
            <p>Bring monitoring, topology, configuration, ticket, and source-of-truth information together so engineers spend less time reconstructing the state of the network during an incident.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Repeatable Automation</h3>
            <p>Automate well-understood operational tasks through controlled workflows rather than treating every recurring check or change as a manual one-off.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Investigation Support</h3>
            <p>Use AI-assisted tooling to help summarize events, surface relevant operational context, and support engineer decision-making without pretending that every incident should be fully autonomous.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section partner-context-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Partner Context</span>
        <h2>ITcare HORA</h2>
        <p>
          ITcare publishes AI NetOps through its HORA platform alongside network architecture, 24/7 NOC, DevOps, and automation services. That makes it relevant when AI-assisted operations need to sit inside a broader production-network operating model rather than as a standalone dashboard.
        </p>
        <a href="/partners/itcare" class="partner-context-link">View ITcare partner profile →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2>Define the Operational Problem First</h2>
        <p>Start with your monitoring stack, incident workflow, source of truth, and the repetitive work you want to reduce.</p>
        <a href="/lets-talk?service=ai-netops" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Discuss AI-Assisted Operations</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-container { max-width: 1040px; }
  .service-header { text-align: left; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 0 64px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .header-badge-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .service-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .service-lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .service-hero-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .section-sub-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .content-section > p { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 780px; }
  .problem-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .problem-card { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .problem-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .problem-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .partner-context-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 40px; }
  .partner-context-link { display: inline-flex; margin-top: 18px; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-blue); }
  .partner-context-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .service-footer-cta { padding: 40px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; gap: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .service-footer-cta p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
</style>
